WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.117
SOC 2 is an auditing and attestation framework developed by the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants, commonly known as the AICPA.

2
00:00:10.117 --> 00:00:18.568
It is used to evaluate whether an organization has designed and operates controls that support one or more Trust Services Criteria.

3
00:00:18.568 --> 00:00:26.171
Those criteria relate to security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality, and privacy.

4
00:00:26.171 --> 00:00:38.414
In everyday language, SOC 2 helps customers understand whether a service provider has practices in place to protect systems, information, and commitments that matter to the customer relationship.

5
00:00:38.414 --> 00:00:52.352
SOC 2 is especially common for technology companies, SaaS providers, cloud services, managed service providers, and other organizations that handle customer data or operate important systems on behalf of others.

6
00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:55.805
A key point is that SOC 2 is not a certification.

7
00:00:55.805 --> 00:00:59.816
It is an independent attestation performed by qualified auditors.

8
00:00:59.816 --> 00:01:08.736
The resulting report describes the audit scope, the criteria included, the controls evaluated, testing performed, and the auditor's opinion.

9
00:01:08.736 --> 00:01:17.017
Customers use SOC 2 reports during vendor reviews, procurement, risk assessments, renewals, and security questionnaires.

10
00:01:17.017 --> 00:01:23.523
The report gives them a structured way to understand how the organization approaches trust and operational control.

11
00:01:23.523 --> 00:01:29.230
For employees, SOC 2 matters because the report is based on real operating practices.

12
00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:38.809
Policies, access controls, change records, monitoring activities, training, incident response, and evidence all come from normal work across the organization.

13
00:01:38.809 --> 00:01:42.411
This course provides an educational overview of SOC 2.

14
00:01:42.411 --> 00:01:48.447
It is not professional legal, accounting, regulatory, assurance, or compliance guidance.

15
00:01:48.447 --> 00:01:53.965
The goal is to help you understand the concepts and your role in supporting trustworthy operations.

16
00:01:53.965 --> 00:01:59.752
The most useful way to think about SOC 2 is as a trust conversation supported by evidence.

17
00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:09.111
The report helps an organization explain what it does, how controls are evaluated, and why customers can place confidence in the services being provided.
